{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/MohamedRejeb/Calf/pulls/541","id":4504728939,"node_id":"PR_kwDOKDql7s8AAAABDIC1aw","html_url":"https://github.com/MohamedRejeb/Calf/pull/541","diff_url":"https://github.com/MohamedRejeb/Calf/pull/541.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/MohamedRejeb/Calf/pull/541.patch","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/MohamedRejeb/Calf/issues/541","commits_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/MohamedRejeb/Calf/pulls/541/commits","review_comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/MohamedRejeb/Calf/pulls/541/comments","review_comment_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/MohamedRejeb/Calf/pulls/comments{/number}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/MohamedRejeb/Calf/issues/541/comments","statuses_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/MohamedRejeb/Calf/statuses/645b80631a7a764aa2f9caaecff3bbc3eae63ece","number":541,"state":"closed","locked":false,"title":"feat(ui): add a cross-platform selectable dates rule to AdaptiveDatePicker","user":{"login":"MohamedRejeb","id":41842296,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQxODQyMjk2","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/41842296?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/MohamedRejeb","html_url":"https://github.com/MohamedRejeb","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MohamedRejeb/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MohamedRejeb/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MohamedRejeb/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MohamedRejeb/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MohamedRejeb/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MohamedRejeb/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MohamedRejeb/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MohamedRejeb/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MohamedRejeb/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"Closes #328.\n\n## Summary\n\nThe docs advertised a `dateValidator` parameter on `AdaptiveDatePicker` that never existed. This adds a real, cross-platform way to restrict which days can be picked.\n\n- `AdaptiveDatePickerState` and `rememberAdaptiveDatePickerState` gain an observable `selectableDates` rule, using Material3's `SelectableDates` interface. It is the only restriction parameter.\n- `DateBounds(minDateMillis, maxDateMillis)` is a `SelectableDates` for a minimum and maximum day, inclusive and compared per UTC day. An infix `and` combines rules, for example `DateBounds(minDateMillis = today) and weekdaysOnly`.\n- **Material**: the Material3 state is wrapped so it reports the caller's rule object. Material3 caches each day's enabled flag keyed on that object, so a rule that changes its answers in place would never redraw.\n- **iOS 16+**: the inline picker is backed by `UICalendarView`. Its selection delegate greys out rejected days, `DateBounds` map to the available date range, and the visible days are rebuilt after every change so it shows immediately rather than on the next scroll or tap.\n- **iOS wheels, and inline below iOS 16**: `UIDatePicker` only supports min/max, so `DateBounds` stop the wheels natively and any other rejected pick snaps to the nearest selectable day.\n- A selection the new rule rejects moves to the nearest selectable day on every platform. The state is the source of truth and the native view follows it.\n- The saver re-attaches the rule and still restores lists saved before it existed. Year bounds use a dependency-free days-to-civil calculation.\n- Docs rewritten with multiplatform examples. The sample shows an inline picker driven by a range chip row and a weekdays-only toggle, plus, on iOS only, a wheels picker to exercise the snapping fallback.\n\nTwo follow-up branches build on this one: `feat/compact-date-picker` and `feat/date-range-picker`.\n\n## Test plan\n\n- [x] `./gradlew :calf-ui:desktopTest` — 33 tests: `DateBoundsTest`, `DateBoundsSelectableDatesTest`, `AdaptiveDatePickerStateMaterialTest`, including Compose tests that re-sync the rule on recomposition and assert a weekend cell becomes disabled after switching to a weekdays-only rule\n- [x] `./gradlew :calf-ui:testDebugUnitTest` — the shared tests on Android\n- [x] calf-ui compiles for Android, iOS device and simulator, Desktop, JS and Wasm; the sample compiles on every target\n- [x] iOS simulator: weekends greyed out with \"Weekdays only\", range chips hide the months outside the range, `UIKitDisplayMode.Wheels` snaps a rejected pick\n- [x] Android: rule and range changes apply immediately without scrolling the calendar\n","labels":[],"milestone":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"created_at":"2026-09-11T09:59:48Z","updated_at":"2026-09-12T10:59:54Z","closed_at":"2026-09-12T10:59:53Z","merged_at":"2026-09-12T10:59:53Z","merge_commit_sha":"e535b7a59347875a468d261e44049bf601315c5e","assignee":null,"assignees":[],"requested_reviewers":[],"requested_teams":[],"head":{"label":"MohamedRejeb:fix/date-picker-selectable-dates","ref":"fix/date-picker-selectable-dates","repo":{"id":674932206,"node_id":"R_kgDOKDql7g","name":"Calf","full_name":"MohamedRejeb/Calf","owner":{"login":"MohamedRejeb","id":41842296,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQxODQyMjk2","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/41842296?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/MohamedRejeb","html_url":"https://github.com/MohamedRejeb","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MohamedRejeb/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MohamedRejeb/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MohamedRejeb/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MohamedRejeb/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MohamedRejeb/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MohamedRejeb/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MohamedRejeb/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MohamedRe